    "plain_text": "Modulo 7, the equation gives 4x ≡ 3 mod 7, so x ≡ 6 mod 7. Write x = 6 + 7t. Substituting gives y = 5 - 4t. The nonnegative constraints force t = 0 or 1, producing (6,5) and (13,1).",
    "markdown": "Modulo $7$, the equation gives $4x \\equiv 3 \\pmod 7$, so $x \\equiv 6 \\pmod 7$. Write $x = 6 + 7t$. Substituting gives $y = 5 - 4t$. The nonnegative constraints force $t = 0$ or $1$, producing $(6,5)$ and $(13,1)$."
